{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld","id":845549,"title":"SO a solar goes wondering into the wyld...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-11T03:47:28-08:00","id":845549,"title":"SO a solar goes wondering into the wyld...","content":"And due to a lack of charms, or lack of vigilance, or lack of caring, eventually the Solar begins to change. How much would a Solar have to change for the exaltation to consider the original host dead and depart from the body, while still technically leaving the original host alive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:56:52-08:00","id":845561,"title":"","content":"They'd have to be completely and utterly inhuman. Every cell in their body, every iota of intelligence would have to be irrevocably warped by the Wyld. Basically, they'd have to be so utterly warped that a Raksha could simply use a Shaping action to kill them. Of course, the ST could decide otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:15:04-08:00","id":845565,"title":"","content":"ST fiat. After all, humans with dolphin bodies are still apparently human enough to Exalt, as are demesne-dwellers whose physical forms have been transmuted into sunlight.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the word you meant in the title was &quot;wandering.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:23:11-08:00","id":845588,"title":"","content":"Generally Exaltations never fall off unless you die. So you have to functionally be dead, wherein your soul falls off, for it to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845565#post845565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think the word you meant in the title was &amp;quot;wandering.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>no","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:44:30-08:00","id":845633,"title":"","content":"In 2e, there was a rule that made your Exaltation vacate the premises if you had too many mutation points. So far, there's no indication that it's still the case in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:15:56-08:00","id":845647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845633#post845633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, there was a rule that made your Exaltation vacate the premises if you had too many mutation points. So far, there's no indication that it's still the case in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>No there wasn't. 1e had an Essence cap based on how many mutation points you had (Willpower - total mutation points) that 2e did away with, in fact. This was probably on account of not having unbalanced stat boosts like Tough (+2 Strength, +1 Stamina, soak lethal with full Stamina and extra health levels... as a mere affliction!), though even late 1e had a rule for buying mutations with bonus points to avoid having them count, which is pretty much the only way that Lunars could get a decent amount of soak from Armor-Forming Technique, as the limit was half Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-11-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:22:56-08:00","id":845674,"title":"","content":"Given the wyld does mutations and weirder things, and given that via directed sorcery there's no limit on the mutations you can grant yourself, I would believe there's no limit on the mutations that a Solar can have from the wyld. Which leaves weirder things.<br /> <br /> I would have no problem with things like &quot;the solar got turned into a kitten&quot; &quot;the solar got turned into a serial killer that kills people every time they hear the word shubbery&quot; or even &quot;the solar got turned into an animated pillar of salt&quot;. Because all those things are still actors able to interact with the environment in a meaningful way<br /> <br /> I would declare them dead if they got turned (long term) into something like a salt statue of themselves (immobile) or a boat, or a forest glen, because at that point they can't meaningfully interact with others or the setting. They are still capable of being seasoning for food, a thing to ride or provide fruit but no more than the perfectly mundane version of those objects.<br /> <br /> Where this gets a slight wrinkle for some people, is that THIS DOES NOT APPLY TO PCs. if a PC gets turned into a salt statue of themselves in the place of the Raksha Ad'oy and her circlemates are running around to seek a cure or treatment, there is still hope and they might be saved. This is my opinion YMMV etc etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The key is less &quot;What is the line at which the Exaltation falls off&quot; and more &quot;Is it dramatically appropriate in this specific situation that the exaltation falls off?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":31,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","user":"Odd_Canuck","date":". 03-11-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:08:00-08:00","id":845692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845647#post845647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No there wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange, I could have sworn there was something like that somewhere in 2e. Sadly, I cannot check it right now, as I don't have access to my 2e books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:07:59-08:00","id":845798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845692#post845692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange, I could have sworn there was something like that somewhere in 2e. Sadly, I cannot check it right now, as I don't have access to my 2e books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall that the hive mutation, if taken to a high-enough level, renders your body into a hollow shell that's nothing more than a puppet controlled by the insects inside. At that point you have no agency and you're basically dead as a macro-organism, even if your flesh continues living on a cellular level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:26:15-08:00","id":845806,"title":"","content":"I'm personally not a fan of any wonkiness that could de-Exalt someone being part of the mainline setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T14:00:53-08:00","id":845821,"title":"","content":"As I recall, the concept of &quot;Exaltation leaves you despite not being dead&quot; was only ever actually stated in those Ebon Dragon Charms to banish somebody from everything forever, as security against the idea of an Essence being permanently removed from the world. Any ideas about the notion of being sufficiently mutated to no longer qualify as human <i>while being Exalted</i> was just a lot of forum extrapolation, helped along by the idea that a First Age Solar was making humans who could have been so mutated that they would never be Exalted in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T20:20:36-08:00","id":845927,"title":"","content":"Any hypothetical speculation like this really needs to be approached from &quot;what serves the needs of a gaming group&quot; to have any value, because any answer that doesn't make for a fun gaming session is not useful.<br /> <br /> If you want an exalted level-monster to hit home to your players what can happen if you wander the Wyld without protection, the answer is that things can get pretty freaky and still be an Exalt.<br /> <br /> f you have a player that wants to weaponize the Wyld to de-exalt people the answer is probably that the circumstances that can cause it are too difficult and complex to arrange for it to be a practical tool, but maybe possible to arrange as a one-off tactic for an otherwise impossible-to-kill enemy.<br /> <br /> If you're planning on using it on a player, that probably depends somewhat on wether you're using it as just a dramatic way of killing a character off, or as part of some sort of redemption arc, where the player loses their power and now has to find some way to regain it (or learn that they don't really need it to make a difference and accomplish their goals). Definitely keep an eye on how to keep things fun for the player you use it on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T21:47:03-08:00","id":845948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barefoot Monkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845798#post845798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that the hive mutation, if taken to a high-enough level, renders your body into a hollow shell that's nothing more than a puppet controlled by the insects inside. At that point you have no agency and you're basically dead as a macro-organism, even if your flesh continues living on a cellular level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That &quot;high enough level&quot; is &quot;more than once&quot;. Taking Hive abomination twice doesn't give you a bigger hive to control; rather you <i>become</i> the hive.<br /> <br /> All the text says about what happens then is that: &quot;Whether the character is still truly alive at that point is a question no one is willing to investigate closely.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T22:17:40-08:00","id":845955,"title":"","content":"I agree with those who've said that it needs to be addressed on a case by case basis depending on what fits your game. Especially since, as I see it, either side of the line has unfortunate implications. If you say the Exaltation sticks around, then you've got people trying to lock Exaltations out of the cycle of reincarnation via shenanigans that are probably harder than simply killing the person. If you say it leaves, then people are going to try to build some kind of De-Exaltation Weapon. The case by case basis thing seems like the best way to go to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T22:41:34-08:00","id":845966,"title":"","content":"Lunar Chimerism and Infernal body horror both illiterate just how tenacious an Exaltation can be. Spend centuries as a maddened, ever-shifting nightmare wandering through the Wyld? That Exaltation is still holding on. Did you transform into an alien god avatar because you wanted some tentacles with mouths that spew acid? Like dogs and donuts, your Exaltation won't judge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T02:13:08-08:00","id":845999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want an exalted level-monster</div> </div> </div> </div> I would be wary of this for the same reason that I dislike the chimera; I don't like the idea of wasting an Exaltation on a generic gribbly monster rather than a figure with actual personality and aspirations to contend with. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That &quot;high enough level&quot; is &quot;more than once&quot;. Taking Hive abomination twice doesn't give you a bigger hive to control; rather you become the hive.</div> </div> </div> </div> A notable part of this is that there's no actual benefit or incentive to a player character taking the mutation enough times to get into that ambiguous territory, leaving it purely in the realm of plot device for people who have had too much exposure to a mutating influence. Still, it's one of the shortcomings of treating Wyld mutation both as a source of mechanically useful things and as a general warping, and trying to categorize these things together based on degree of transformation rather than actual utility. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Chimerism</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:32:41-08:00","id":846081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845999#post845999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A notable part of this is that there's no actual benefit or incentive to a player character taking the mutation enough times to get into that ambiguous territory</div> </div> </div> </div>No extra benefit, sure; but I'd argue that playing as a walking hive-with-a-skin is itself the incentive. I mean, I'd play it, and play up the whole demon-anathema angle...<br /> <br /> This gives me an idea for a sorcerer... *scribbles wildly on a character sheet*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:49:22-08:00","id":846090,"title":"","content":"&quot;I made myself a hive for freaky hornet-spirits&quot; does sound like a pretty cool initiation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:50:46-08:00","id":846093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846081#post846081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No extra benefit, sure; but I'd argue that playing as a walking hive-with-a-skin is itself the incentive. I mean, I'd play it, and play up the whole demon-anathema angle...<br /> <br /> This gives me an idea for a sorcerer... *scribbles wildly on a character sheet*</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do so as well if I could come up with a mutant concept that I'd actually like and doesn't just feel random. but most of the mutations just don't seem substantial enough. like its a thing I want, but the mutation selection just doesn't feel like enough y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:34:00-08:00","id":846276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=845927#post845927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any hypothetical speculation like this really needs to be approached from &amp;quot;what serves the needs of a gaming group&amp;quot; to have any value, because any answer that doesn't make for a fun gaming session is not useful.<br /> <br /> If you want an exalted level-monster to hit home to your players what can happen if you wander the Wyld without protection, the answer is that things can get pretty freaky and still be an Exalt.<br /> <br /> f you have a player that wants to weaponize the Wyld to de-exalt people the answer is probably that the circumstances that can cause it are too difficult and complex to arrange for it to be a practical tool, but maybe possible to arrange as a one-off tactic for an otherwise impossible-to-kill enemy.<br /> <br /> If you're planning on using it on a player, that probably depends somewhat on wether you're using it as just a dramatic way of killing a character off, or as part of some sort of redemption arc, where the player loses their power and now has to find some way to regain it (or learn that they don't really need it to make a difference and accomplish their goals). Definitely keep an eye on how to keep things fun for the player you use it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to think of ways that a PC might get to encounter the consciousness of their past incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:51:10-08:00","id":846285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846276#post846276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to think of ways that a PC might get to encounter the consciousness of their past incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:30:00-08:00","id":846388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846285#post846285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they do that? every time people keep suggesting this, I keep thinking of a mad scientist Twilight who just does for fun while laughing maniacally without any rhyme or reason! so theoretically, anything can be done with A Sorcerous Working. thats not the problem. its coming up with the WHY anyone would use a sorcerous working to do something, thats the real problem. because.....<br /> <br /> wait......why would need to be done by the........CURRENT Solar? why not.....a sorcerous working to make sure the NEXT person who gets your Exaltation also gets to encounter your consciousness? NOW we have a reason, one of the last Solars of the Usurpation might've used a Sorcerous Working to save their own consciousness so that they're taken along for the ride with the next person to be Exalted....because while the new guy might be in control, the previous Solar would be able to at least act as some Avatar-style spirit guide....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:37:43-08:00","id":846397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they do that?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's like going on an online forum to ask for somebody's reasoned opinion (or even expert one, if you're very lucky), but a bit more substantive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:03:30-07:00","id":846524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846285#post846285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous Working.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would require active involvement on the part of the PC - I want to arrange an accidental meeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:19:09-07:00","id":846532,"title":"","content":"They can get dreams and visions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:36:46-07:00","id":846607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846524#post846524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would require active involvement on the part of the PC - I want to arrange an accidental meeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>In no way does it need to be the PC's sorcerous working. It could be the prior incarnation's, or one of their friends', or a Gold Faction Sidereal trying to teach new Solars by invoking their righteous ancestors. I mean hell it's not like you have to tell the PC exactly how this is happening :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:02:38-07:00","id":846688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846388#post846388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">every time people keep suggesting this, I keep thinking of a mad scientist Twilight who just does for fun while laughing maniacally without any rhyme or reason!</div> </div> </div> </div>And? Just because you personally don't see a reason doesn't mean no reason exists.<br /> <br /> Maybe an Exalt needs or wants to know something his prior incarnation knew. Or evokes a past self to satisfy Amalion, for instance. Any number of reasons could exist, though admittedly quite a few would be specific to a given gaming group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-13-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T01:00:43-07:00","id":846964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/845549-so-a-solar-goes-wondering-into-the-wyld?p=846276#post846276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was trying to think of ways that a PC might get to encounter the consciousness of their past incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. There's probably lots of ways to pull this off, actually. The most commonly used one is typically to have them run into the ghost of their former exaltation who's still kicking around the underworld. Or you could have the players run into an artifact (humanoid and/or animate, or not) that their former self imbued with a perfect copy of their conciousness. With the Wyld, being a source of strangeness that it is, you could just have the characters meet someone who seemingly is their past-life self, still living! Is he from an alternate Creation somewhere out there in the Wyld where the Usurpation never happened? Does he just believe he is, but was simply created from the chaos ex nihilo with memories to fit? Is it actually some strange Wyld spirit that simply disguises itself by reading and mimicing the past life memories of the Exalted it encounters? The reality is, you wouldn't even need to have an answer, if it's not something the players have any practical way of finding out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}